        "title": "fix(sqlite): canonicalize migration target aliases",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- canonicalize trusted session SQLite migration target paths before archive safety checks\n- preserve symlink rejection while accepting macOS root aliases such as `/tmp` to `/private/tmp`\n- add a macOS regression test and changelog entry\n\n## Root cause\n\nPlanned archive moves were canonicalized, but repeated target inputs remained lexical. On macOS isolated QA state rooted under `/tmp`, the source path became `/private/tmp` while the target stayed `/tmp`, so Gateway startup falsely rejected its own legacy store as outside the sessions directory.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/test-projects.mjs src/commands/doctor-session-sqlite.test.ts`\n- 52/52 tests passed\n- structured Codex autoreview: clean\n- isolated private QA Gateway advanced past session SQLite migration\n",
